{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>תגל.</b> From the nif'al paradigm." "<b>ולא אפגע אדם.</b> \"And I will not accept the entreaty of a man,\" like ואל תפגע בי (Jeremiah 7:16), as an intercession. Now if there were a bet after the word פגיעת, it would be the one acted upon. Some say: \"I will take vengeance from you, and I will not meet with a man,\" like ויפגעו את משה ואת אהרן (Exodus 5:20) — that he stand in my way, or that he say to me, 'Do not do it'; or: לא אפגע אדם — that I will not rejoice [at any man]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {1 "Resolved פיוס as 'intercession' based on parallel with Jeremiah 7:16; the comparison hinges on the meaning of פגיעה as entreaty/intercession."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:24.171950938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}